{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>A king, etc.</b> These are the words of the prophet, as if saying: Judah will remember when the messengers of the king of Assyria came to take tribute from Hezekiah, for he gave all the treasuries of the house of HaShem, and he punished all Judah, and they would say: Who will go with us from Hezekiah's officers to the king of Assyria with this tribute — 'a king in his beauty shall your eyes behold; they shall see a land of distances' — for Assyria is far from Jerusalem."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:31.016769928Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}